# Kalshi BTC 1-Hour Bot — Cursor Context

You are working on `kalshi_btc_1hr_bot/`, a Python framework for forecasting
Kalshi KXBTCD hourly binary contracts on BTC BRTI settlement.

## Market
- Series: KXBTCD (hourly only, filter out daily buckets)
- Window: 3600 seconds
- Settlement: 60-second BRTI average at top of hour
- Strike K = BRTI at window open

## 5-Layer Model (model.py)
1. GBM core with 60s averaging vol adjustment
2. Multi-TF momentum (5m/15m/30m weighted blend)
3. Funding rate signal (Binance perp)
4. Mean reversion toward VWAP
5. Volatility regime (low/med/high confidence weighting)
Final: logistic calibration on 18 features

## Trading Rules
- min_edge: 2.5 cents (0.025)
- Kelly: 20% fraction, 4% max bankroll per trade
- Daily loss stop: 6%
- Cycle: 5 seconds
- Default: PAPER mode, NO TRADE when edge insufficient

## Key Files
- config.py — all tunable parameters
- data_feed.py — Binance spot + funding + momentum/VWAP
- model.py — 5-layer ensemble
- edge.py — EV calculation with Kalshi fees
- sizing.py — fractional Kelly
- risk.py — bankroll caps, drawdown stop
- backtest.py — synthetic backtest (no API keys)
- bot.py — main paper/live loop

## Commands
- make setup && source .venv/bin/activate
- make backtest (synthetic)
- make paper-once (single cycle)
- make paper (continuous)

## Do NOT
- Promise 75-80% win rates
- Trade without clearing min_edge
- Skip paper mode for initial testing
